// mayhem/iptables_shim.go.src — a tiny stdlib-only stand-in for
// github.com/openyurtio/openyurt/pkg/util/iptables, staged by mayhem/build.sh
// into the _mayhem_harness/iptables mini-module at iptables/iptables.go.
//
// WHY: pkg/util/iptables/testing/parse.go's ONLY non-stdlib import is openyurt's
// own pkg/util/iptables, and from it parse.go uses exactly TWO symbols — the
// string types `iptables.Table` and `iptables.Chain` (see the `grep iptables.`
// audit in build.sh: only Table/Chain type conversions, no funcs/constants).
// The real package drags in k8s.io/apimachinery + k8s.io/klog + k8s.io/utils
// (sets, version, wait, exec, trace), which would pull openyurt's entire
// Kubernetes go.mod closure into the mini-module and defeat the point of
// isolating a dependency-light surface. These two named string types are
// behaviorally identical for parse.go's use (plain conversions + string
// comparison), so the parsed dump/rule structures AND the oracle's exact values
// are exactly what upstream produces. build.sh's sed only repoints parse.go's
// import path at this shim; parse.go itself is copied verbatim (minus the
// package rename).
package iptables

// Table represents an iptables table name (matches upstream's `type Table string`).
type Table string

// Chain represents an iptables chain name (matches upstream's `type Chain string`).
type Chain string
